 "title": "The Carnot cycle between 500 °C and 20 °C",
 "caption": "1 mol of monatomic gas runs A→B isothermally at T_h = 773 K (500 °C), B→C adiabatically, C→D isothermally at T_c = 293 K (20 °C), D→A adiabatically. Heat in Q_h = nRT_h ln(V_B/V_A) = 4.5 kJ, heat out Q_c = 1.7 kJ, so Q_c/Q_h = T_c/T_h and η = 1 − 293/773 = 62%. Net work (enclosed area) 2.8 kJ.",
 "alt": "p–V diagram of a Carnot cycle: a hot isotherm A to B, an adiabat B to C, a cold isotherm C to D and an adiabat D to A; efficiency 62 percent.",
 "description": [
  "Axes: volume in litres, pressure in MPa, for 1 mol.",
  "A→B: isothermal expansion at 773 K from 1 L to 2 L, absorbing Q_h = 4.5 kJ.",
  "B→C: adiabatic expansion to 8.6 L, cooling to 293 K (TV^(γ−1) is constant, γ = 5/3).",
  "C→D: isothermal compression at 293 K to 4.3 L, rejecting Q_c = 1.7 kJ.",
  "D→A: adiabatic compression back to A. η = W/Q_h = 2.8/4.5 = 62% = 1 − T_c/T_h."
